WEBVTT

NOTE v3 English captions for Warrior Two. Soft Jenny voice, phonetic Sanskrit.

1
00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:03.402
This is Warrior Two.

2
00:00:04.102 --> 00:00:09.142
In Sanskrit it is called veer ah bah drah sah nah two.

3
00:00:10.042 --> 00:00:15.610
Once more, slowly: veer ah bah drah sah nah two.

4
00:00:16.810 --> 00:00:20.218
Here is what this pose is for.

5
00:00:20.918 --> 00:00:24.614
It can build strength in the legs.

6
00:00:25.164 --> 00:00:28.116
It helps open the hips.

7
00:00:28.666 --> 00:00:33.682
And it is a way to practice a wide, steady stance.

8
00:00:34.582 --> 00:00:38.998
Please be careful if your front knee feels sore.

9
00:00:39.548 --> 00:00:45.236
Keep that knee over the ankle, and pointing toward your small toe.

10
00:00:46.336 --> 00:00:55.024
Mirror me. We will take the left foot forward, that is the foot on the left side of your screen.

11
00:00:56.024 --> 00:01:02.672
Step one. From standing, step your feet wide apart.

12
00:01:03.372 --> 00:01:09.564
Keep both legs straight, and both feet pointing forward for a moment.

13
00:01:10.464 --> 00:01:21.192
Step two. Turn your left foot out 90 degrees, toward the left end of the mat, and turn your right foot in a little.

14
00:01:21.892 --> 00:01:25.996
Keep both legs straight while the feet turn.

15
00:01:26.896 --> 00:01:34.240
Step three. Bend your left knee, and stack it over your left ankle.

16
00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:43.744
Then lift both arms to shoulder height, palms facing down, as if you were reaching toward both ends of the room.

17
00:01:44.744 --> 00:01:51.872
Step four. Turn your head and look out over your left fingertips.

18
00:01:52.572 --> 00:01:59.244
Keep your chest open to the long side of the mat, and keep your torso upright.

19
00:02:00.244 --> 00:02:03.628
Breathe in to lift and lengthen.

20
00:02:04.828 --> 00:02:10.684
Breathe out to settle, only as far as the front knee stays comfortable.

21
00:02:11.884 --> 00:02:20.188
A common mistake: do not let the front knee fall in, and do not lean the torso out over the front thigh.

22
00:02:21.188 --> 00:02:28.364
An easier version: step the feet a little closer, and bend the front knee less.

23
00:02:29.064 --> 00:02:34.128
If your shoulders tire, rest the back hand on your hip.

24
00:02:35.128 --> 00:02:46.144
Hold for about thirty to forty-five seconds. Then straighten the front leg, lower your arms, and step your feet together.
